---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Photo from "../components/Photo.astro";
import Testimonials from "../components/Testimonials.astro";
import CallToAction from "../components/CallToAction.astro";
import { business } from "../config/business";
import { person } from "../lib/schema";

const crumbs = [{ name: "About", path: "/about/" }];
const yearsInTrade = new Date().getFullYear() - business.foundedYear;
---

<Base
  title="About Dixon Masonry | Mason in Lake Geneva, WI"
  description="Brent Dixon has run Dixon Masonry in Lake Geneva since 2001. A family trade, carried on, with stone artistry and a standard that does not move."
  path="/about/"
  crumbs={crumbs}
  schema={[person()]}
>
  <div class="container">
    <Breadcrumbs crumbs={crumbs} />
  </div>

  <article>
    <header class="head container">
      <h1>The mason you will actually be dealing with</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Dixon Masonry is {business.owner.fullName}. He has been in the trade
        since {business.foundedYear}, which is {yearsInTrade} years of laying
        stone around this lake.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="container split">
      <div class="prose">
        <h2>A trade that was handed down</h2>
        <p>
          Masonry came to Brent through the family. That matters more than it
          sounds, because the things that separate good stonework from average
          stonework are not in a manual. They are judgement calls about which
          face of a stone goes out, how wide a joint should read, when to stop
          and recut. You learn those standing next to someone who already knows.
        </p>

        <h2>He works the job himself</h2>
        <p>
          Brent is on site doing the work. When a job is big enough to need
          more hands he brings on additional crew, but he is the one laying
          stone and the one you talk to. There is no estimator who hands you
          off, and no crew arriving to build something they were not part of
          quoting.
        </p>
        <p>
          The practical upshot is that nothing gets lost in translation. What
          you agreed is what gets built, because the same person did both.
        </p>

        <h2>Every project is personal</h2>
        <p>
          This is a small enough town that reputation is the only marketing
          that works. Brent takes on work he can do properly and turns down
          work he cannot, which is why he will sometimes tell you a repair is
          not worth doing or that a job should wait until spring. It costs him
          a booking and saves you money, and it is the reason people call back
          years later.
        </p>

        <h2>Insured, local, and not going anywhere</h2>
        <p>
          Dixon Masonry is insured. Brent works Lake Geneva and the
          communities around the lake, and does not travel into Illinois. If
          you want to see work in person before committing, ask. There is a
          good chance something is standing near you.
        </p>
        <p>
          <a href="/lake-geneva-masonry/">See the full list of areas served</a>,
          or <a href="/gallery/">look through the stonework gallery</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="side">
        <Photo
          name="11-team/dixon-masonry-crew"
          sizes="(min-width: 64em) 32vw, 100vw"
          widths={[400, 640, 900]}
        />
        <p class="caption">
          Brent with crew on a residential job. There is no studio headshot,
          which feels about right for someone who is on a scaffold most days.
        </p>

        <dl class="facts">
          <div>
            <dt>Established</dt>
            <dd>{business.foundedYear}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Based</dt>
            <dd>{business.address.locality}, {business.address.region}</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Specialism</dt>
            <dd>Stone masonry and stone artistry</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Insurance</dt>
            <dd>Insured</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>

        <Photo
          name="07-commercial/mason-hand-cut-brick"
          sizes="(min-width: 64em) 32vw, 100vw"
          widths={[400, 640, 900]}
        />
      </aside>
    </div>

    <div class="container reviews">
      <Testimonials
        slugs={["review-3", "review-7"]}
        heading="In customers' words"
      />
    </div>
  </article>

  <CallToAction
    heading="Want to talk it through with Brent directly?"
    body="No call centre and no sales visit. You describe the job, he tells you what it involves and what it is likely to cost."
    primaryLabel="Send Brent a message"
  />
</Base>

<style>
  .head {
    padding-block: var(--space-6) var(--space-7);
  }

  .head h1 {
    max-width: 20ch;
  }

  .head .lead {
    margin-block-start: var(--space-5);
  }

  .split {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-8);
    align-items: start;
    padding-block-end: var(--section-y);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64em) {
    .split {
      grid-template-columns: 1.6fr 1fr;
      gap: var(--space-9);
    }
  }

  .side {
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-5);
  }

  @media (min-width: 64em) {
    .side {
      position: sticky;
      top: 7rem;
    }
  }

  .caption {
    margin-block-start: calc(var(--space-3) * -1);
    font-size: var(--text-sm);
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .facts {
    margin: 0;
    padding: var(--space-5);
    background: var(--bg-subtle);
    border: 1px solid var(--border);
    border-radius: var(--radius);
    display: grid;
    gap: var(--space-4);
  }

  .facts div {
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }

  .facts dt {
    font-size: var(--text-xs);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--text-faint);
  }

  .facts dd {
    margin: 0;
    font-size: var(--text-base);
  }

  .reviews {
    padding-block-end: var(--section-y);
  }
</style>
